§ `Sections 748 to 749 -- Pardons and remissions`

-- src:16258 | 748 (1) Her Majesty may extend the royal mercy to a person who is sentenced to imprisonment under the authority of an Act of Parliament, even if the person is imprisoned for failure to pay money to another person.
@ref s 748(1) (src:16258)
GIVEN `the person is sentenced to imprisonment under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 748(1) Her Majesty may extend the royal mercy to the person, even if the person is imprisoned for failure to pay money to another person` MEANS
    IF `the person is sentenced to imprisonment under the authority of an Act of Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is sentenced to imprisonment under the authority of an Act of Parliament"

DECLARE `s 748(2) kind of pardon` IS ONE OF
    `s 748(2) a free pardon`
    `s 748(2) a conditional pardon`
    `s 748(2) a pardon of another kind`

-- src:16260 | (2) The Governor in Council may grant a free pardon or a conditional pardon to any person who has been convicted of an offence.
@ref s 748(2) (src:16260)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      pardon IS A `s 748(2) kind of pardon`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 748(2) the Governor in Council may grant the pardon` MEANS
    IF `the person has been convicted of an offence` AND NOT (pardon EQUALS `s 748(2) a pardon of another kind`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may grant a free pardon or a conditional pardon to any person who has been convicted of an offence"

-- src:16262 | (3) Where the Governor in Council grants a free pardon to a person, that person shall be deemed thereafter never to have committed the offence in respect of which the pardon is granted.
@ref s 748(3) (src:16262)
GIVEN `the Governor in Council grants a free pardon to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is the offence in respect of which the pardon is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 748(3) the person is deemed thereafter never to have committed the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Governor in Council grants a free pardon to the person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Governor in Council grants a free pardon to a person, that person shall be deemed" (a "where" gate, ruling (b))
        IF `the offence is the offence in respect of which the pardon is granted` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "never to have committed the offence in respect of which the pardon is granted"

-- src:16264 | (4) No free pardon or conditional pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment to which the person might otherwise be lawfully sentenced on a subsequent conviction for an offence other than that for which the pardon was granted.
@ref s 748(4) (src:16264)
GIVEN `the pardon is a free pardon or a conditional pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent conviction is for an offence other than that for which the pardon was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 748(4) the pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment to which the person might otherwise be lawfully sentenced on the subsequent conviction` MEANS
    IF `the pardon is a free pardon or a conditional pardon` AND `the subsequent conviction is for an offence other than that for which the pardon was granted`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No free pardon or conditional pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment ... on a subsequent conviction for an offence other than that for which the pardon was granted" (fork F-15)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a subsequent conviction for an offence other than that for which the pardon was granted"

-- src:16266 | 748.1 (1) The Governor in Council may order the remission, in whole or in part, of a fine or forfeiture imposed under an Act of Parliament, whoever the person may be to whom it is payable or however it may be recoverable.
