§ `Section 750 -- Disabilities`

-- src:16274 | 750 (1) Where a person is convicted of an indictable offence for which the person is sentenced to imprisonment for two years or more and holds, at the time that person is convicted, an office under the Crown or other public employment, the office or employment forthwith becomes vacant.
@ref s 750(1) (src:16274)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      sentence IS AN Imprisonment
      `the person holds, at the time of the conviction, an office under the Crown or other public employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is convicted of an indictable offence`)) OR (NOT (`the person holds, at the time of the conviction, an office under the Crown or other public employment`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an indictable offence ... and holds, at the time that person is convicted, an office under the Crown or other public employment" (a "where" gate, ruling (b))
        OTHERWISE `s 742.1 the sentence of imprisonment is at least that many years` sentence 2   -- JUST TRUE for two years or more, JUST FALSE under two years ("sentenced to imprisonment for two years or more"), NOTHING when no term is stated

DECLARE `s 750(2) capacity` IS ONE OF
    `s 750(2) holding any office under the Crown or other public employment`
    `s 750(2) being elected as a member of Parliament or of a legislature`
    `s 750(2) sitting or voting as a member of Parliament or of a legislature`
    `s 750(2) exercising any right of suffrage`
    `s 750(2) another capacity`

-- src:16276 | (2) A person to whom subsection (1) applies is, until undergoing the punishment imposed on the person or the punishment substituted therefor by competent authority or receives a free pardon from Her Majesty, incapable of holding any office under the Crown or other public employment, or of being elected or sitting or voting as a member of Parliament or of a legislature or of exercising any right of suffrage.
@ref s 750(2) (src:16276)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A `s 750(2) capacity`
      `the person has undergone the punishment imposed on the person or the punishment substituted for it by competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has received a free pardon from Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (1) applies to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person to whom subsection (1) applies"
        IF `subsection (1) applies to the person` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): subsection (1) is not decided on these facts
        IF `the person has undergone the punishment imposed on the person or the punishment substituted for it by competent authority` OR `the person has received a free pardon from Her Majesty`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until undergoing the punishment imposed on the person or the punishment substituted therefor by competent authority or receives a free pardon from Her Majesty" (the "until" bar: gone)
        IF capacity EQUALS `s 750(2) another capacity` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names four capacities and does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16278 | (3) No person who is convicted of
-- src:16279 | (a) an offence under section 121, 124 or 418,
-- src:16280 | (b) an offence under section 380 committed against Her Majesty, or
-- src:16281 | (c) an offence under paragraph 80(1)(d), subsection 80(2) or section 154.01 of the Financial Administration Act,
-- src:16282 | has, after that conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty or to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person or to hold office under Her Majesty.
@ref s 750(3) (src:16278-16282)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence under section 380 was committed against Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence under paragraph 80(1)(d), subsection 80(2) or section 154.01 of the Financial Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is convicted of the offence`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person who is convicted of ..."
        IF (elem (offence's `section`) (LIST 121, 124, 418)) OR ((offence's `section` EQUALS 380) AND `the offence under section 380 was committed against Her Majesty`) OR `the offence is an offence under paragraph 80(1)(d), subsection 80(2) or section 154.01 of the Financial Administration Act`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person who is convicted of ... has, after that conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty or to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person or to hold office under Her Majesty" (a flat negative; the capacities may be restored under subsections (4) and (5))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) an offence under section 121, 124 or 418, (b) an offence under section 380 committed against Her Majesty, or (c) an offence under paragraph 80(1)(d), subsection 80(2) or section 154.01 of the Financial Administration Act"

-- src:16284 | (4) A person to whom subsection (3) applies may, at any time before a record suspension for which he or she has applied is ordered under the Criminal Records Act, apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of one or more of the capacities lost by the person by virtue of that subsection.
@ref s 750(4) (src:16284)
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record suspension for which the person has applied is ordered under the Criminal Records Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(4) the person may apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of one or more of the capacities lost` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`subsection (3) applies to the person`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person to whom subsection (3) applies"
        IF `a record suspension for which the person has applied is ordered under the Criminal Records Act`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before a record suspension for which he or she has applied is ordered under the Criminal Records Act" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16286 | (5) Where an application is made under subsection (4), the Governor in Council may order that the capacities lost by the applicant by virtue of subsection (3) be restored to that applicant in whole or in part and subject to such conditions as the Governor in Council considers desirable in the public interest.
@ref s 750(5) (src:16286)
GIVEN `an application is made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions are such as the Governor in Council considers desirable in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(5) the Governor in Council may order that the capacities lost be restored, in whole or in part, subject to conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application is made under subsection (4)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made under subsection (4), the Governor in Council may order" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `the conditions are such as the Governor in Council considers desirable in the public interest` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to such conditions as the Governor in Council considers desirable in the public interest" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16288 | (6) Where a conviction is set aside by competent authority, any disability imposed by this section is removed.
@ref s 750(6) (src:16288)
GIVEN `the conviction is set aside by competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
