§ `Sections 751 to 751.1 -- Costs to the successful party in a case of libel`

-- Section 751 is stated as an entitlement ("is entitled to recover"). The name carries "entitled", so the function is listed in the fork register, group (ii):
-- this part answers NOTHING outside the scope the text sets, and the other reading is JUST FALSE.
-- src:16292 | 751 The person in whose favour judgment is given in proceedings by indictment for defamatory libel is entitled to recover from the opposite party costs in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court.
@ref s 751 (src:16292)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings by indictment for defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment is given in the person's favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751 the person in whose favour judgment is given is entitled to recover costs from the opposite party` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings by indictment for defamatory libel` AND `judgment is given in the person's favour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The person in whose favour judgment is given in proceedings by indictment for defamatory libel" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c); an "entitled"-named function, group (ii))

-- src:16292 | 751 The person in whose favour judgment is given in proceedings by indictment for defamatory libel is entitled to recover from the opposite party costs in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court.
@ref s 751 (src:16292)
GIVEN `the amount is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is fixed by order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751 the costs are in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court` MEANS
    IF `the amount is reasonable` AND `the amount is fixed by order of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "costs in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court"

-- src:16294 | 751.1 Where costs that are fixed under section 751 are not paid forthwith, the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs by filing the order in any civil court of the province in which the trial was held that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount, and that judgment is enforceable against the opposite party in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against that opposite party in that court in civil proceedings.
@ref s 751.1 (src:16294)
GIVEN `the costs are fixed under section 751` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are not paid forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is filed in a civil court of the province in which the trial was held that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751.1 the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the costs are fixed under section 751`)) OR (NOT (`the costs are not paid forthwith`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where costs that are fixed under section 751 are not paid forthwith" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `the order is filed in a civil court of the province in which the trial was held that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by filing the order in any civil court of the province in which the trial was held that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

